<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Orleans.Dataflow.Samples</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Server is the silo meta-package: Runtime, the Sdk with its code generator, and the in-memory grain
      storage the cluster scenario registers the coordinator's state provider over. It is what a deployment
      references to host a silo, which is the point — the cluster scenario is meant to be readable as the
      registration an operator writes rather than as a test fixture. Nothing test-only is referenced
      anywhere in this application, deliberately: the samples are also the evidence that the public API is
      enough on its own.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Orleans.Server" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/Orleans.Dataflow/Orleans.Dataflow.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/Orleans.Dataflow.Orleans/Orleans.Dataflow.Orleans.csproj" />
    <!--
      The F# half of the sample, holding the F# authoring of every scenario and the small kernel both
      frontends share. Both authorings must run in one process, because comparing them is the whole point,
      so one of the two has to be a library and the other the application that drives it.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../Orleans.Dataflow.Samples.FSharp/Orleans.Dataflow.Samples.FSharp.fsproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
